# queue_and_tree, the whole program in ONE cell, Unicon entry, developer_15 2026-11-22. THE LAW OF EACH STEP, worked out from the program and unicon 13.3's own image() BEFORE any run:
# records print record node_1(2), the object object Queue_1(1), an integer 7, null &null; build creates a node BEFORE it recurses, so the root is node_1, n1 node_2, n11 node_3, n12 node_4, n2 node_5, n21 node_6, n22 node_7;
# the breadth-first visits are n, n1, n2, n11, n12, n21, n22, the nodes 1, 2, 5, 3, 4, 6, 7, and seen counts 1 to 7. The breakpoint is the visit's write (line 36), inside the loop of walk: a break near the top of a long cell is lost by the driver (said to the cao).
# A step in at the every of line 37 enters Queue_push, the frame Unicon names it, with the item the first kid; a step out of it leaves the every's other pushes behind it (they are the same depth, never a stop) and stops at the while head, line 33, the turn of the back edge after the every ends (the cto's ruling 2026-11-25: a loop of n turns stops at its head n+1 times, so the head is a stop here).
{"break": [0, 36]}
